# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# External integration engineers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A partner's engineer writing a payment adapter never needs to see the ledger,
# and the port is what makes that true: `PayoutProvider` is five methods and
# none of them exposes financial state. So an adapter folder can be theirs
# while everything above stays ours.
#
# Add the contractor's handle to their own adapter directory when an engagement
# starts, e.g.:
#
#   /packages/adapters/src/paycrest/  @rogerpanel @their-handle
#
# The catch-all `*` rule above still requires an owner's review on every pull
# request, so this widens who may *write* a directory, never who may merge it.
#
# None of this takes effect until branch protection is enabled on the working
# branch with "require review from Code Owners". CODEOWNERS on its own is
# documentation. See docs/DECISION_STABLECOIN_ROUTE.md §4.

# The port definitions are read-only to a contractor: changing the shape of the
# boundary is a decision about the whole system, not about one provider.
/packages/adapters/src/ports/ @rogerpanel
